                       [«· ToyDay by Joo/Toytools ·»]

                  Today's uploads counter for DayDream BBS

                          Version 1.0  [01-Apr-97]


  Introduction
  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯
  ToyDay is a small utility which counts today's uploaded bytes & files.
  It's especially meant to be used with ToyJoin (joinconf-door), but if you
  find any other usage for it, go ahead.


  Requirements
  ~~~~~~~~~~~~
  Requires a running (Amiga) DayDream BBS.


  Installation
  ~~~~~~~~~~~~
  You can put this tool anywhere but I suggest "DayDream:Utils".


  Configuration
  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  Then you need to make a configuration file which is just a text file which
  can have four types of keywords in it.
  
     %nF   outputs uploaded files in conference [n].      (e.g. "%2F")
     %nB   outputs uploaded bytes in conference [n].      (e.g. "%8B")
     %nK   outputs uploaded kilobytes in conference [n].  (e.g. "%13K")
     %nM   outputs uploaded megabytes in conference [n].  (e.g. "%9M")

  If you use ToyDay with ToyJoin, use ANSI-codes to jump to the right place
  at the screen. Then use the keywords to output number of uploaded files,
  bytes etc. You don't have to put all conferences in the config, e.g. just
  put those which are public and have fileareas or maybe edit own configs
  for certain access levels.


  Usage
  ~~~~~
  USAGE: ToyDay <CONFIGFILE> <OUTPUTFILE>

  Run ToyDay in DayDream's logoff batch or somewhere where it will be
  updated after each user or upload.

  Example:

     DayDream:Utils/ToyBytes DayDream:Configs/ToyBytes.CFG DayDream:Display/ISO/ToyDay.GFX

  Then just display the outputfile in ToyJoin (add a line to ToyJoin.GFX):

     ÿBDayDream:Display/ISO/ToyDay.GFX|


